# On Teaching a Fractured Macroeconomics.

**Authors:** Galbraith, James K.

## Abstract
Offers an analysis of the Joint Council's &quot;Framework for Teaching Basic (Economic) Concepts&quot; in the area of macroeconomics. Suggests that the &quot;Framework&quot; be altered to include economic history, competing macro economic theories, and the great economic theorists and the problems they faced. Concludes that students must learn that macroeconomics is closer to a moral philosophy than a science. (JDH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ356154

